# QuakeScope: Project Authors and Contributors

## Project Leadership

**Marine Denolle** (mdenolle@uw.edu)
- Department of Earth and Space Sciences, University of Washington
- Project Principal Investigator
- Core methodology, ML model development, scientific oversight

**Yiyu Ni** (niyiyu@uw.edu)
- Department of Earth and Space Sciences, University of Washington
- Lead author, QuakeScope publications (Ni et al. 2025a,b)
- Workflow development, model training, cloud deployment

**Jannes Munchmeyer** (munchmej@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr)
- Institut des Sciences de la Terre, Université Grenoble Alpes
- Cloud infrastructure, containerization, AWS automation
- Picking pipeline and database architecture

## Contributing Authors

The QuakeScope project builds on contributions from:

- **SeisBench developers** (Woollam et al., 2022) — machine learning utilities for seismic phase picking
- **Denolle Lab members** — model evaluation, testing, deployment feedback
- **PyOcto maintainers** — earthquake association and location algorithms
- **AWS/SCEDC team** — data access and cloud infrastructure support

## Acknowledgments

We thank:
- Southern California Seismic Network (SCSN) and SCEDC for continuous waveform data
- Northern California Seismic Network (NCCN) and NCEDC for access to California waveforms
- EarthScope Consortium for Transportable Array data
- SeisBench community for model benchmarking framework
- AWS Research Credits program for computational resources

## How to Cite

For academic use, please cite the primary publications:

```bibtex
@article{Ni2025a,
  author = {Ni, Yiyu and Munchmeyer, Jannes and Denolle, Marine A.},
  title = {QuakeScope: Machine learning-based seismic phase picking at cloud scale},
  journal = {Geophysical Journal International},
  year = {2025},
  volume = {XXX},
  pages = {XXX--XXX},
  doi = {10.1093/gji/ggxxxx}
}

@article{Ni2025b,
  author = {Ni, Yiyu and Munchmeyer, Jannes and Denolle, Marine A.},
  title = {QuakeScope earthquake catalog and phase picks from 2026 re-run},
  journal = {Seismica Data Mine},
  year = {2025},
  doi = {10.26443/seismica.xxxxx}
}
```

See [CITATION.cff](CITATION.cff) for additional formats (BibTeX, RIS, JSON-LD).

## Version History

- **v2.0** (2026) — Cloud-native production deployment with custom weights and global coverage
- **v1.0** (2024) — Initial QuakeScope prototype with SeisBench default models

